= EAR

== Function
- Hearing and balance.
- Beautification.

== Nerves and Anatomy
- Nerve: Vestibulocochlear nerve (8th cranial nerve).
- Part in the ear - balance.
- External ear:
  - Pinna.
  - External acoustic meatus / External auditory canal.
- Middle ear:
  - Middle ear cleft.
- Inner ear:
  - cochlea.
  - vestibule.

== Middle Ear Cleft Contents
- 2 muscles:
  - Tensor tympani.
  - Tensor veli palatini.
- 3 Bones:
  - Malleus.
  - incus.
  - stapes.
- Set of artery nerve.
- Set of vein.
- Parts included in middle ear cleft:
  - Attic.
  - aditus.
  - mastoid antrum.
  - mastoid aircells.
  - middle ear cavity.
  - tympanic membrane.
  - eustachian tube.

== Types of Hearing Loss
- Conductive: up to middle ear.
- Sensory neural: inner ear tract.
- Mixed variety.
- Course of conductive type of hearing loss:
  - Impacted wax - most common.
- Presbicosis:
  - It is sensory type of hearing loss.
  - Due to aging process.

== Cranial Nerves Note
- Olfactory nerve - tract, relay station.
- বাকি সব Cranial nerve - নার্ভ।

== Auricle / Pinna
- 1 piece of fatty elastic cartilage.
- Bone - type II collagen fiber.
- Pericondritis:
  - lat. 1/3 of Ext. auditory canal.
- S/F (Signs/Symptoms) of pericondritis:
  - pain.
  - fever.
  - ear fullness.
  - referred otalgia.
- Complication of pericondritis:
  - Cauliflower like / butt ear / boxer ear.
- Causative organism:
  - Pseudomonas.
- Pathophysiology:
  - pus form ez Blood - neutrophilic leukocyte.
  - Neutrophil numerous, short half life, easily adhere.
- Treatment:
  - ceftazidine, ceftriaxon IV.
  - ciprofloxacin - during discharge - oral.
  - Analgesic.
  - Viniger soak gause.

== Furunculosis
- Causative organism: staph aureus.
- Auditory canal infection.
- Staph aureus in nose - vestibulitis.
- Skin Abscess / boil.
- Otoscope contraindicated.
- thirdicup contraindicated - vestibulitis.
- Drug of choice:
  - Flucloxacillin 500mg 6 hourly & TDS - 7 days.
- Symptoms & Signs:
  - Severe pain, discomfort in the ear.
  - Conductive hearing loss.
- Diagnostic:
  - Severe tragal tenderness.
  - Pinna pull up - severe pain.

== Sinusitis and Pathology
- Air fluid level - Acute sinusitis.
- hazyness - chronic sinusitis.
- Investigation: X-Ray of nose and paranasal sinus, occipito-mental view.
- Pathology of vocal cord (Horseness of voice):
  - polyp.
  - cyst.
  - nodule.
  - unilateral paralysis of vocal cord.
- Most common cause of horseness of voice: laryngitis.
- Adv (Advice):
  - Avoide of talking.
  - avoid galgel.

== Otorrhoea and Ear Conditions
- Short Case: Examine the ear.
- Otorrhoea: due to any kind of infection.
- CSOM.
- 100% normal tympanic membrane: cone of light present.
- Mixed type of hearing loss: odiogram / odiometry.
- X-ray naso-pharynx lateral view for Adenoid.
- Abscess:
  - Localized collection of pus.
  - in a confined space.
  - surrounded by a pyogenic membrane.
- C/S - report আসে 72 hrs পর।
- ASOM: Acute suppurative otitis media.
- CSOM: Chronic suppurative otitis media.

== Eustachian Tube
=== Function
- ventilation.
- Equilibrium to the nasopharynx middle ear cavity.
- Clearance of middle ear secretion.
- Maintain pressure b/w middle ear cavity & nasopharynx.

=== Difference in Child & Adult
- length:
  - child: 18mm (short).
  - Adult: 36mm (double).
- position:
  - child: More horizontal.
  - Adult: vertical / oblique.
- width:
  - child: wider.
  - Adult: naroo.

=== Progression
- ASOM - বেশি হয় school going children এ।
- consequence হল CSOM.
- tympanic membrane (intact) -> CSOM -> perforation.
- tympanic mem. develop ৩ germ layer থেকে।

== ASOM Causes and Lymph Nodes
- Cause of ASOM (organism):
  - Strep pneumonia.
  - Hemo influenza.
  - pseudomonus.
  - staph aureus.
  - E. coli.
- predisposing factor:
  - upper respiratory tract info (child, old).
  - Immunocompromized Pt.
- Lymph nodes:
  - Approx. 800 lymph node.
  - neck এ 300.
- peritonsilar abeess - Adult (unilateral).
- Ch. tonsilitis - Children (bilateral).

== Treatment Protocols
- Antibiotic acc. to C/S (broad spectrum).
- Analgesic, PPI.
- Antihistamin - to reduce secretion.
- Blue baby - Ampicillin.
- Grey baby - Cloramphenicol.
- Red man syndrom - vencomicin.
- topical ear drop with steroid.
- Nasal decongestion for eustachian tube.

== CSOM Varieties
- 2 type:
  - Tubotympanic.
  - Atticoantral.
- Tubotympanic:
  - Mucosal varity.
  - safe varity.
  - Extratemporal / Intratemporal.
- Atticoantral:
  - squamosal varity.
  - unsafe varity / dangerous.
  - Dangerous due to presence of cholestetoma causes bone errosion.
- bone erossion by these enzyme:
  1. collagenase.
  2. Protease.
  3. Acid phosphatase.
  4. Hyaluronidase.
- Stages:
  - Active Stage: More sign & symptom, tm congested.
  - Inactive stage: tm pale.
- Cholesteatoma:
  - abnormal growth of Keratinizing squamous epitheliom in middle ear.

== Tubo-tympanic Variety
- Affected area: Eustachian tube + tympanic cavity/mem.
- Presentation:
  - Intermittent otorrhoea.
  - Intermittent aural discharge.
  - Hearing impairment.
  - Pain, fever, vertigo.
- perforation - central.
- Parts affected: pars tensa part of tympanic membrane, pars flacida.
- characteristic of central perforation:
  - disruptead of pars tensa.
  - Rest of the tm intact.
  - Anular lig. intact.
- charecteristics of pus in tubo tympanic:
  - thin.
  - profuse.
  - non-malaudarous.
  - muco-purulent/serous/whitish.
  - intermilen.

== Complication of Tubo-tympanic variety
=== Extra cranial / Intratemporal
- Facial nerve palsy (most common).
- Mastoiditis.
- Post-auriculate abeess.
- Bezold abeess.
- Digestig abeess.
- Para-parannageal abcess.
- Petrocitis.
- Laryerinthitis.

=== Intra-cranial
- Otogenic brain abeess (Most common).
- Subdural abeers.
- Extra-dural abeers.
- Meningitis.

=== Management of active stage of tubo-tyup
- tarjet - inactive করব, then surgery করব.
- Medications:
  - Antibiotic.
  - Antihistarnin - decrease secretion.
  - Nasal deppccongestion for functing of Eustachion tube.

== causes of Eustachian tube dysfunction
1. Upper respiratory tract infection.
2. Allergy (type 1 hypersensiti).
3. Enlarge adenoid.
4. Cleft palate.
5. Hypothyroidism.
6. CA of nasopharynx.
7. Smoaking.

== Surgery Notes
- Timing:
  - Inactive হওয়ার 6-12 wks পর surgery করব।
  - cz tympanic membrane এর healing / streangth আসতে 6-12 wks লাগে.
- Myringoplasty: Repair of tympanie membrane.
- Jympanoplasty:
  - Erradication of middle ear disease.
  - Reassuration of hearing mechanism with/without repain of tm.
- type 1 - Repair of tm.
- Myringoplasty = type 1 tympanoplasty. এটার type আছে-tympanoplasty.

== Myzing oplasty
=== Aim of Myringoplasty
1. Prevent recurrent otorrhoea.
2. Increase quality of life.
3. Improvement of hearing.

=== Investigation before surgery
- Tests: Pure tone audiometry - Audiogram, tympanogram.
- Reasons:
  - documentation.
  - Medicolegal purpos.
  - function of M.E.
  - Type & degree of hearing loss-by audiogram.
  - Post operative purp assessment.

=== Pre-requisite of myringoplasty
1. Age > 10 years (repeted infection due to cold).
2. 2 faicting ear must present.
3. Entorchian tube must be functioning.
4. Ear should be dry for 6-12wks.

=== Approach & Graft
- Approach:
  - Post arienlas incision.
  - Transcanal endscopic of External auditory camar.
- Graft for tympanoplasty:
  1. Jemporalis fascia - most common.
  2. Jagal perichonbrium cartilage.
- 90% - temporalis fascia cause:
  - Graft can taken by same incision.
  - Thin tough structure like tympanic membrane.
  - low metabolic rate.
- Type of graft:
  1. Auto - Same person.
  2. Iso - Pdentical twin.
  3. Allo - Same species.
  4. Xeno - Another species.
- operative microscope lens:
  1. Myringoplasty - 250mm.
  2. MLE - Mierolaringeal excision - 400mm.

== Complication of Myringoplasty
1. Graft rejection.
2. loss of taste sensation of ant 2/3 - due to injury to the condae tympany branch of facial nerve.
3. Injury to jingular valve - bleeding.
4. Dislocation of Makis, ineus, Stapes.

== Nerve Supply
